{"id": "3fd715ac-a03b-4489-83c0-eac78519853c", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "This is really a knowledge question about SageMaker Feature Store encryption defaults rather than something requiring an AWS call—without a KmsKeyId specified in S3StorageConfig, offline store data defaults to SSE-S3 encryption rather than a customer-managed KMS key, and I should also consider what's happening with the online store config.

So without a KmsKeyId specified, this offline store falls back to default SSE-S3 encryption rather than a customer-managed KMS key—still encrypted at rest, but that may or may not satisfy a policy requiring CMK usage. I also can't tell from this response alone whether the bucket itself enforces a different default encryption, and the online store isn't evaluated here since no OnlineStoreConfig was given.

